"privacy" = "Privacy";
"privacy_detail" = "Reports are saved only after preview and your explicit request. No upload or telemetry.";
"privacy_local_body" = "NetUnstick has no accounts, advertising, analytics, tracking or background uploads. Network observations are processed on this Mac. Device names, SSIDs, addresses, internal domains, credentials and packet contents are omitted or redacted from history and reports.";
"privacy_local_title" = "Local processing";
"privacy_network_body" = "On your request, diagnostics resolve example.com using your resolver, connect to 1.1.1.1:443 and browse local Bonjour services. A device test contacts the endpoint you entered. DNS providers and contacted devices can see the usual network metadata, including the source address. No diagnostic report is sent to the developer. When update checks are enabled, the app fetches a version file from itorg.pl at startup. You can turn this off. A PKG is downloaded after you click. Hosting receives normal HTTP metadata, including your IP address, but no reports or device identifier.";
"privacy_network_title" = "Network traffic";
"privacy_permissions_body" = "You can cancel checks and revoke Local Network access in System Settings. The full edition also lets you unregister its helper. Exporting or sharing a report is optional. Information you choose to send to a support provider is handled by that recipient.";
"privacy_permissions_title" = "Your choices";
"privacy_retention_body" = "Local history holds at most 20 sessions, 100 entries per session and 4 MB, including times, app/macOS versions, outcome and error codes and sanitized evidence. Delete it in Settings. Reports are saved only after a preview and your choice of file; delete exported copies separately. macOS manages the retention of its private system log entries.";
"privacy_retention_title" = "Storage and deletion";
"privacy_version_body" = "23 October 2026. Publisher: ITORG Krzysztof Radzimski. Privacy contact: kr@itorg.pl.";
"privacy_version_title" = "Policy version";
